==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1432.  From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|topographye|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|topographia|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|τοπογραφία||tr=topographia|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|τόπος||place|tr=topos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|γράφω||I write|tr=graphō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/təˈpɒɡɹəfi/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/t@"pQgr@fi/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/təˈpɑɡɹəfi/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/t@"pAgr@fi/}}
* {{hyphenation|top|og|raphy}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|topographies}}

# a [[precise]] [[description]] of a [[place]]
# a [[detail]]ed [[graphic]] [[representation]] of the [[surface]] [[feature]]s of a place or [[object]]
# the features themselves (the [[terrain]])
# the [[surveying]] of the features

